<title>GEORGIA: BA to begin London-Tbilisi passenger route.</title>
<headline>BA to begin London-Tbilisi passenger route.</headline>
<dateline>TBILISI 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways will begin regular, thrice-weekly flights between London and the Georgian capital Tbilisi on April 14, a senior Georgian aviation official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Zurab Chankotadze, chairman of the Georgian State Aviation Agency, told Reuters that BA would operate a 124-seat A-320 jet on the route.</p>
<p>He said Georgia's state airlines did not plan to fly to Britain.</p>
<p>Only one foreign carrier, Turkish Airlines, makes regular passenger flights to Tbilisi.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
